; Minimal startup prototype, not an installed Thread service.
; Priming contract: fresh zeroed Thread, canonical entry frame at Start,
; CR1 = application's E-GT; c-list Boot.Thread = supervisor Thread GT.
; Application entry is first public method (CLOOMC selector #0).
; No heap allocator/checkpoint ABI.
; Mint-side protected-frame priming is a fixture prerequisite, not implemented here.
abstraction ide.AmoebaStartup {
capabilities {
    SELF E,
    ide.CapabilityTest E,
    ide.ActorManager E,
    Thread.2
}
method Start {
    ; Boot starts Amoeba in Thread 1.
    ; Amoeba calls the simplified CapabilityTest—no CHANGE or SWITCH.
    ; CapabilityTest calls SelfTest, which returns, then WukongCallHome, which returns.
    ; CapabilityTest returns to Amoeba, rather than looping internally.
    ; Amoeba starts the Alice/Mallory attack.
    ; The attack triggers the expected HardFault.
    ; The fault/reboot path restarts the entire sequence.
    Init:
    ; Initialize application-visible startup status in the current Thread.
    IADD DR1, DR0, #0
    ; Ordinary CALL checks the supplied application's Enter authority.
    CALL ide.CapabilityTest, Run
    ; Application returns here; preserve its DR1 result and yield to supervisor.
    ; CALL/RETURN does not preserve scratch CR2: reload declared authority.
    ; LOAD CR2, CR6, #1
    CHANGE Thread.2
    ; A completed startup must not restart the application if resumed.
    BRANCH Init
}
}
